         "step": 1,
         "text": "A degree 2 polynomial needs the values through order 2: \\( g(3) = 4 \\), \\( g'(3) = -2 \\), \\( g''(3) = -1 \\). The value of order 3 is not used.",
         "mathjson": -1
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Divide each by the matching factorial: \\( \\frac{4}{0!} = 4 \\), \\( \\frac{-2}{1!} = -2 \\), \\( \\frac{-1}{2!} = -\\frac{1}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
